---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { APP_STORE, rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
import { appStoreCampaignUrl, LAST_HUMAN_ASC_TOKENS } from '../../lib/campaignLinks.mjs';
const description = `Privacy policy for Last Human: Dodge the Bots by ${LEGAL_NAME}.`;
const appStoreHref = appStoreCampaignUrl(APP_STORE.lastHuman, LAST_HUMAN_ASC_TOKENS.privacy);
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · Last Human: Dodge the Bots" description={description} path="/privacy/last-human">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last Human: Dodge the Bots · Effective date: September 21, 2026</p>

      <p>
        <strong><a href={appStoreHref}>Last Human is available on the App Store.</a></strong>
        This policy describes version 1.0 as shipped.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        {LEGAL_NAME} operates Last Human, a free arcade game supported by ads. There are no accounts,
        and your progress, high scores, settings, and purchase state stay on your device. The app sends
        limited anonymous usage analytics through PostHog and anonymous crash reports through Sentry.
        Google AdMob serves non-personalized ads. None of these services is used to track you across
        other companies' apps or websites.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your unlocked floors, stars, high scores, and other gameplay progress.</li>
        <li>Your app settings, analytics preference, and Remove Ads purchase state.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is stored locally on your device. We do not receive your score, progress map,
        or anything you type. Deleting the app removes its local app data from your device; App Store
        purchase records remain with Apple so eligible purchases can be restored.
      </p>

      <h2>Usage analytics (PostHog) — on by default, Settings opt-out</h2>
      <p>
        Last Human sends a small set of product events: app opened, floor started, completed, or failed,
        Remove Ads purchased or restored, and Settings opened. The events use bounded values such as a
        floor number, attempt-count range, star count, and failure reason. They do not include free text,
        exact scores, your progress map, transaction IDs, advertising identifiers, or contact information.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Analytics uses a random, app-specific installation ID shown in Settings. It is not tied to a
          Dudley account because Last Human has no accounts.
        </li>
        <li>
          Turn off <strong>Share anonymous usage analytics</strong> in Settings to stop new events,
          clear the unsent queue on your device, and discard that ID. Turning analytics back on creates
          a new ID.
        </li>
        <li>
          Sent events are retained for <strong>90 days</strong> as individual records and up to
          <strong>13 months</strong> as aggregated statistics. To request deletion of sent events, copy
          the Analytics ID before turning analytics off and email
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Crash reporting (Sentry)</h2>
      <p>
        If Last Human crashes, Sentry can receive an anonymous crash report containing the stack trace
        and coarse technical details such as the app version, iOS major version, device class, and
        lifecycle state. Crash reporting does not include a user profile, screenshots, view hierarchy,
        gameplay progress, scores, or advertising state. Crash reports are retained for
        <strong>30 days</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
      <p>
        Interstitial ads can appear on the corporate memo screen between floors, never during gameplay.
        One optional rewarded ad can also let you continue a run. Ads are served by
        <strong>Google AdMob</strong>, a third-party advertising network. Last Human requests
        <strong>non-personalized</strong> ads, does not request Apple's cross-app tracking permission,
        and does not request ads in the EEA or UK. Google may still process device, coarse location,
        ad-interaction, performance, and diagnostic information to provide and measure ads. Dudley does
        not join that information with the app's analytics or use it to build a profile of you.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          How Google uses this data is described in
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google's advertising policy</a> and
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          A one-time Remove Ads purchase at the price shown in the app removes between-floor
          interstitial ads. The optional watch-to-continue ad remains available once per run.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Used to track you</h2>
      <p>
        None of the data described on this page is used to track you across other companies' apps or
        websites, linked to your identity, or combined with data from a data broker. We do not sell
        your personal data.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Last Human is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from
        anyone under 13. The app has no accounts, profiles, chat, or in-app messaging.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the new version will be posted at this URL with an updated
        effective date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or a data request? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
